l no dry flour remains. Leave the lumps: overmixing makes flat, tough pancakes. Let the batter rest while the pan heats, {time 5 min}.","uses":[]},{"text":"Heat the skillet or griddle over medium heat, or set an electric griddle to {temp 375F}. Brush it lightly with oil. It is ready when a drop of water sizzles and skitters across the surface.","uses":[8]},{"text":"Pour about {qty 1/4 cup fixed} of batter per pancake, leaving room between them. Cook until bubbles cover the surface and the edges look dry and set, {time 2-3 min}.","uses":[]},{"text":"Flip with a thin spatula and cook until the underside is golden and the center springs back when pressed, {time 1-2 min}.","uses":[]},{"text":"Repeat with the remaining batter, brushing the pan with a little more oil between rounds. Lower the heat slightly if the pancakes brown before bubbles form. Serve hot with maple syrup.","uses":[8,9]}]}